@lang en
IMPORT `baominh-par-claim`

-- Tests for layer 2: how much. Every expected value was worked by hand from the clause cited
-- beside it, before the assertion was run; the arithmetic is written out. All amounts are
-- scenario values in VND (baominh-par-fixtures.l4 says why). The building's sum insured is
-- 1,000,000,000; the Schedule's deductible is 10,000,000 for each loss.

§ `Tests: the amount`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN i IS A `A damaged item`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount for` i MEANS
    `the amount for the item` i `given` (`the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` i) i)

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of property`
      v IS A `The valuation of the item`
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a fire damaging` k `valued` v MEANS
    `an item of` k `damaged by` (LIST `directly` fire) `in` `the ordinary circumstances` `valued` v

GIVEN v IS A `The valuation of the item`
GIVETH A `The valuation of the item`
`with other insurance of 1,000,000,000` v MEANS `The valuation of the item` WITH
    `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss`                      IS v's `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss`
    `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded`        IS NOTHING
    `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss`            IS v's `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss`
    `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss`   IS LIST 1000000000
    `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS NOTHING
    `the costs of the media`                                          IS NOTHING

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The valuation of the item`
`Damage of 100,000,000 with a marine policy paying` m MEANS `The valuation of the item` WITH
    `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss`                      IS 100000000
    `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded`        IS NOTHING
    `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss`            IS JUST 1000000000
    `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss`   IS EMPTY
    `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS m
    `the costs of the media`                                          IS NOTHING

GIVEN mc IS A MAYBE `The costs of electronic data processing media`
GIVETH A `The valuation of the item`
`media valued with` mc MEANS `The valuation of the item` WITH
    `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss`                      IS 999
    `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded`        IS NOTHING
    `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss`            IS JUST 1000000000
    `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss`   IS EMPTY
    `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS NOTHING
    `the costs of the media`                                          IS mc

GIVEN r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The costs of electronic data processing media`
`blank media 2,000,000 and copying 3,000,000, restored` r MEANS `The costs of electronic data processing media` WITH
    `the cost of blank media`                                         IS 2000000
    `the cost of copying the data from back-up or from the originals` IS 3000000
    `the media are repaired, replaced or restored`                    IS r

§§ `The measure of the Damage (insuring clause, src:16-17)`

-- 100,000,000 of Damage to a building worth exactly its sum insured: 100,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 1000000000)) EQUALS 100000000

§§ `General Condition 14: average`

-- worth 2,000,000,000 against a sum insured of 1,000,000,000: 100,000,000 x 1/2 = 50,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 2000000000)) EQUALS 50000000
-- worth 1,250,000,000: 100,000,000 x 1,000/1,250 = 80,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 1250000000)) EQUALS 80000000
-- the edge: worth exactly the sum insured, no average ("lớn hơn", greater than)
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 1000000000)) EQUALS 100000000
-- one dong over the sum insured: average bites, just
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 1000000001)) LESS THAN 100000000
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 1000000001)) GREATER THAN 99999999
-- no actual value in the record: refused, by name
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`The valuation of the item` WITH `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss` IS 100000000, `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded` IS NOTHING, `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss` IS NOTHING, `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss` IS EMPTY, `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS NOTHING, `the costs of the media` IS NOTHING)) BECAUSE "the actual value of the item at the time of the loss is not in the record"

§§ `General Condition 6: contribution`

-- another policy of 1,000,000,000 on the same property: 100,000,000 x 1,000/(1,000 + 1,000) = 50,000,000 (fork F16)
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`with other insurance of 1,000,000,000` (`Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 1000000000))) EQUALS 50000000
-- with average as well (worth 2,000,000,000): 100,000,000 x 1/2 x 1/2 = 25,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire damaging` buildings `valued` (`with other insurance of 1,000,000,000` (`Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 2000000000))) EQUALS 25000000

§§ `Exclusion 9: the excess over a marine policy`

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`marine stock with the marine policy paying` m MEANS
    `an item of` stock `damaged by` (LIST `directly` fire) `in` (`circumstances with` (LIST marine)) `valued` (`Damage of 100,000,000 with a marine policy paying` m)

-- the marine policy would pay 80,000,000: the excess is 20,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`marine stock with the marine policy paying` (JUST 80000000)) EQUALS 20000000
-- it would pay more than the Damage: nothing
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`marine stock with the marine policy paying` (JUST 120000000)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount for` (`marine stock with the marine policy paying` NOTHING) BECAUSE "what the marine policy would pay is not in the record"

§§ `Exclusion 10(b): electronic data processing media`

GIVEN mc IS A MAYBE `The costs of electronic data processing media`
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`burnt media with` mc MEANS `a fire damaging` `electronic data processing media` `valued` (`media valued with` mc)

-- restored: blank media 2,000,000 + copying 3,000,000 = 5,000,000 (not the 999 of the general valuation)
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`burnt media with` (JUST (`blank media 2,000,000 and copying 3,000,000, restored` TRUE))) EQUALS 5000000
-- not restored: the blank media only, 2,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`burnt media with` (JUST (`blank media 2,000,000 and copying 3,000,000, restored` FALSE))) EQUALS 2000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount for` (`burnt media with` NOTHING) BECAUSE "the costs of the electronic data processing media are not in the record"

§§ `The part not excluded (exclusions 1(a), 1(c), 8(h))`

-- latent defect and fire both direct; the adjuster puts 30,000,000 of 100,000,000 down to the fire
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`an item of` buildings `damaged by` (LIST `directly` `latent defect`, `directly` fire) `in` `the ordinary circumstances` `valued` (`Damage of` 100000000 `, of which not excluded` 30000000 `, to property worth` 1000000000)) EQUALS 30000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount for` (`a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `directly` `latent defect`, `directly` fire)) BECAUSE "the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded is not in the record"
-- wholly excluded: nothing to measure
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `directly` `latent defect`)) EQUALS 0

§§ `The proviso, limb (i): what is left of the item's sum insured`

GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a fire in a building already paid` p `, with Damage of` d MEANS `A damaged item` WITH
    `the item insured`                  IS `a scheduled item` "factory building" `insured for` 1000000000 `with paid already` p
    `kind`                              IS buildings
    `the chain of causation`            IS LIST (`directly` fire)
    `circumstances`                     IS `the ordinary circumstances`
    `valuation`                         IS `Damage of` d `to property worth` 1000000000
    `what the Insured told the Insurer` IS `nothing false was said`
    `changes under General Condition 8` IS EMPTY
    `claimed as a cost of changing or adding to a computer system, programme, software or chip` IS FALSE

-- 900,000,000 already paid on the building this period: of 500,000,000 only 100,000,000 is left
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire in a building already paid` 900000000 `, with Damage of` 500000000) EQUALS 100000000
-- nothing paid yet: the whole 500,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for` (`a fire in a building already paid` 0 `, with Damage of` 500000000) EQUALS 500000000

§§ `General Condition 13: the deductible, for each loss, after everything else`

-- 100,000,000 less the deductible of 10,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for the loss` `the Schedule` (LIST 100000000) EQUALS 90000000
-- no deductible stated in the Schedule: nothing deducted
#ASSERT `the amount for the loss` `the Schedule without a deductible` (LIST 100000000) EQUALS 100000000
-- below the deductible: nothing; at it: nothing; one dong over it: one dong
#ASSERT `the amount for the loss` `the Schedule` (LIST 5000000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount for the loss` `the Schedule` (LIST 10000000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount for the loss` `the Schedule` (LIST 10000001) EQUALS 1
-- two items in one loss bear one deductible: 60,000,000 + 40,000,000 - 10,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount for the loss` `the Schedule` (LIST 60000000, 40000000) EQUALS 90000000
-- the policy's total sum insured (1,500,000,000) caps the loss before the deductible (fork F14)
#ASSERT `the amount for the loss` `the Schedule` (LIST 1000000000, 1000000000) EQUALS 1490000000
-- the item cap binds first, then the deductible: 100,000,000 left on the item, less 10,000,000 (fork F14)
#ASSERT `the amount for the loss` `the Schedule` (LIST (`the amount for` (`a fire in a building already paid` 900000000 `, with Damage of` 500000000))) EQUALS 90000000

§§ `General Condition 11: reinstatement`

#ASSERT `the most the Insurer is bound to spend reinstating` `the building` `at a cost of` 1200000000 EQUALS 1000000000
#ASSERT `the most the Insurer is bound to spend reinstating` `the building` `at a cost of` 300000000 EQUALS 300000000
#ASSERT `what the Insurer pays where regulations prevent reinstatement` 250000000 EQUALS 250000000
